WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.600
Comm has been found only in some insects.

2
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.520
So how does a mammalian axon stay deaf until it crosses?

3
00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:12.443
The fly has one slit gene.

4
00:00:13.423 --> 00:00:17.763
Mice have three, and two conventional Robo receptors, Robo1 and Robo2.

5
00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:24.367
Earlier work found that mice lacking Slit1 and Slit2 had no defect in commissural

6
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.367
axon guidance.

7
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.457
In 2004, researchers removed all three.

8
00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:31.417
Use the three questions.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:33.537
What should the axons do?

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.940
With no Slit, there is no Slit push, though other cues remain.

11
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.640
The axons still reach the midline, drawn by netrin.

12
00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:49.433
Many stalled in the floor plate.

13
00:00:50.393 --> 00:00:51.833
Others crossed and then turned back.

14
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:54.657
Next, a culture experiment.

15
00:00:55.717 --> 00:01:00.497
Zou and colleagues grew pieces of embryonic rat spinal cord, called explants, in a

16
00:01:00.497 --> 00:01:01.497
gel.

17
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.990
Dorsal explants gave axons that had not yet crossed.

18
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.210
Explants that kept the floor plate gave axons that had crossed.

19
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:12.983
Each kind sat beside cells releasing Slit2.

20
00:01:13.823 --> 00:01:15.123
Which axons should Slit affect?

21
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:24.373
Slit2 held back the growth of axons that had crossed.

22
00:01:25.413 --> 00:01:27.773
Axons that had not crossed were not held back.

23
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:32.517
These were different axons, not one axon before and after.

24
00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:36.417
Still, crossing goes with a change in the response to Slit.

25
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.530
So what keeps a mammalian axon deaf before it crosses?

26
00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.710
An unusual member of the Robo family, called Robo3.

27
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.970
In 2004, it was found on commissural axons before they cross.

28
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.830
Remove Robo3 from a mouse.

29
00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.510
Slit is present. Robo1 and Robo2 are still made.

30
00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.430
Predict.

31
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.900
Almost no commissural axons cross.

32
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.760
They approach the floor plate and turn away.

33
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.720
They hear Slit too early.

34
00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:14.693
That resembles the fly comm mutant.

35
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:19.787
But Robo3 does not clear Robo1 and Robo2 from the surface.

36
00:02:20.687 --> 00:02:23.087
It blunts their response while they stay in the membrane.

37
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.810
Comm lowers Robo1 by sorting, and in at least one other way.

38
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.750
Robo3 mutes it.

39
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.770
Mammals also clear some Robo1.

40
00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:38.010
Proteins called Ndfip1 and Ndfip2 send it to be degraded before crossing.

41
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:41.583
Two splice forms of Robo3 matter here.

42
00:02:42.423 --> 00:02:45.803
In mouse, the form present before crossing disappears afterwards.

43
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:51.437
A second form appears on crossed axons and helps keep them from recrossing.

44
00:02:52.317 --> 00:02:55.237
Mammalian Robo3 has a second job too.

45
00:02:56.097 --> 00:03:00.217
It works with the netrin receptor DCC and strengthens netrin attraction.

46
00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.327
The same gene matters in people.

47
00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:09.647
Mutations in human Robo3 cause horizontal gaze palsy with progressive scoliosis.

48
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.990
In patients, motor and sensory pathways that normally cross in the brainstem appear

49
00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:16.990
uncrossed.

50
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:22.483
The takeaway: mammals both mute their Robo receptors and clear some of them, until

51
00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:23.583
the axon has crossed.
